parts.text:
A long, straight wire P carries a current into the page, as shown in Fig. 6.1.

{{figure:figure_6_1}}

On Fig. 6.1, draw four field lines to represent the magnetic field around wire P due to the current in the wire.

parts.part_stem:
A second long, straight wire Q, carrying a current of $5.0\ \text{A}$ out of the page, is placed parallel to wire P, as shown in Fig. 6.2.

{{figure:figure_6_2}}

The flux density of the magnetic field at wire Q due to the current in wire P is $2.6\ \text{mT}$.
